course: dictionary
lesson: 8146
title: Reptile: a cold-blooded animal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A reptile is a cold-blooded animal with a backbone and dry, scaly skin. Most reptiles lay eggs. Snakes, lizards, turtles, tortoises, crocodiles and alligators are all reptiles.
explain: Cold-blooded does not mean unfriendly. It means the animal cannot make its own body heat, so a reptile warms up by lying in the sun. «Reptiles' dry, scaly skin keeps water in their bodies, so many can live in deserts.» The words dry and scaly are clues to what a reptile's skin is like.
explain: Reptiles are one group of animals with a backbone, along with mammals, birds, amphibians and fish. «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Frogs and crocodiles can look alike, so check the group before you decide.
fact: A reptile is a cold-blooded animal with a backbone.
fact: «Reptiles have dry, scaly skin that keeps water in, and their eggs have a tough shell, so they can live far from water, even in deserts.»
fact: Reptiles cannot make their own body heat, so they warm up by lying in the sun.
fact: Some reptiles, such as certain snakes, are dangerous: leave them alone and back away.
fact: «Dinosaurs had legs straight under the body»; flying and swimming reptiles do not count as dinosaurs.
exercise: What is a reptile? | *A cold-blooded animal with a backbone and dry, scaly skin | A warm-blooded animal with thick fur | A bird that cannot fly | A fish that lives in a lake
exercise: Why do reptiles lie in the sun? | To grow fur | To lay their eggs in the sand | *To warm up, because they cannot make their own body heat | To cool down in the water
exercise: «Frogs, toads, newts and salamanders are amphibians; snakes, lizards, crocodiles and turtles are reptiles.» Which animal is a reptile? | Newt | Frog | *Crocodile | Toad
test: Which of these is NOT a reptile? | Lizard | Alligator | Tortoise | *Frog
test: Why can many reptiles live in deserts? | They swim in the sand | They drink from the sky | They have thick fur to stay cool | *Their dry, scaly skin keeps water in their bodies
exam: Which statement about reptiles is true? | Reptiles are always warm-blooded | *Reptiles have dry, scaly skin | Reptiles have thick fur to keep warm | Reptiles make their own body heat
